1:# Mortgage Calculator: Boilerplate Plan (v2)
3:Status: **boilerplate complete and published** (initial commit `c520f4a` on `main` and `dev`). No mortgage logic exists yet; feature work is tracked in GitHub (see section 9).
6:## 1. Decisions (defaults, change any before approval)
11:| D2  | Package manager         | **Yarn 4 (Berry)** via Corepack, `packageManager` pinned in `package.json`, `.yarnrc.yml` with `nodeLinker: node-modules`    | Node-modules linker keeps Vite, Biome and Husky working without PnP quirks. Say so if you want Yarn 1 (classic) |
12:| D3  | Prod serving (no nginx) | `yarn start` runs `yarn build && serve -s dist -l ${PORT:-3000}`. Docker prod runs the same static server as a non-root user | `serve` is a small static server with SPA fallback. `vite preview` is documented as not for production          |
16:| D7  | Lazy loading            | Layout, every route and heavy features. Not tiny leaf components                                                             | Lazy leaf components cause request waterfalls and hurt LCP. Say so if you want literally everything lazy        |
17:| D8  | Git                     | `git init` (folder isn't a repo), needed by Husky                                                                            | Husky prerequisite                                                                                              |
23:### Yarn Berry gotchas the plan accounts for
25:- Yarn 2+ **does not run `pre*`/`post*` hooks on user scripts**, so there is no `prestart`. `start` chains `yarn build &&` explicitly.
26:- Yarn 2+ **does not run `prepare`**, so Husky installs via `"postinstall": "husky"`. Docker builds set `HUSKY=0` so the hook install doesn't fail without `.git`.
28:## 2. Target layout
39:│   ├── layouts/
40:│   │   └── MainLayout.tsx         # <Outlet/> in Suspense; slot for future <Navbar/>
44:│   │   ├── ui/                    # Tailwind primitives (Button, Card)
64:## 3. Scripts (package.json)
69:| `build`       | `tsc -b && vite build`                                            |
70:| `start`       | `yarn build && serve -s dist -l ${PORT:-3000}`                    |
86:## 4. Code-style rules enforced by Biome
92:**Risk, stated honestly:** Biome has no built-in "components must be arrow functions" or "must have a default export" rule. Rules 1 and 2 need **GritQL plugins** (`biome-plugins/*.grit`, registered under `plugins` in `biome.json`). Plugin support and syntax depend on the Biome version, and "file must contain a default export" is an absence check that Grit may not be able to express. Agent Ember must prove each rule fires on a deliberately bad fixture. If a rule can't be expressed, Ember reports it and proposes the closest enforceable rule (for example, banning `export default function` and `export const Foo =` in component files). Ember does not silently skip it.
94:## 5. Agents and models
98:**Workers: all Sonnet.** Each is defined in `.claude/agents/<name>.md` with `model: sonnet`, a distinct `color`, and a codename, so they show up distinguishable in the terminal. The Agent tool can't set a color per call, so the definition files carry it. New agent definitions may need a session restart to load.
110:### Ownership (exclusive write; no agent touches another's files)
115:| **atlas**       | everything under `src/`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | ember done         | Layout renders routes; each route and the layout is its own chunk; `lint`, `typecheck`, `build` pass; every component follows §4                          |
116:| **harbor**      | `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.dockerignore`                                                                                                                                                                                                               | ember done         | Stages `deps` → `dev` (runs `yarn dev`) → `build` → `prod` (production deps only, `serve`, non-root, `HUSKY=0`). `docker build` passes for both targets   |
118:| **gauge**       | none                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | atlas, harbor done | Reports pass/fail for `yarn install --immutable`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`, chunk list, `docker build` (skipped if Docker absent), bad-commit blocked |
120:### CVE scouts (no `yarn audit` / `npm audit`)
130:## 6. Orchestrator protocol
145:5. Final report: layout, resolved versions, CVE table, verification results, deviations, open issues.
147:## 7. Tradeoff notes (for the final write-up)
150:- **LCP/FCP.** Tiny entry chunk (router plus loader); layout and pages load on demand; Vite emits `modulepreload`; Tailwind ships only used CSS; system font stack.
155:## 8. Approval needed
160:## 9. Feature roadmap (GitHub)

