69:| `build`       | `tsc -b && vite build`                                            |
70:| `start`       | `yarn build && serve -s dist -l ${PORT:-3000}`                    |
86:## 4. Code-style rules enforced by Biome
92:**Risk, stated honestly:** Biome has no built-in "components must be arrow functions" or "must have a default export" rule. Rules 1 and 2 need **GritQL plugins** (`biome-plugins/*.grit`, registered under `plugins` in `biome.json`). Plugin support and syntax depend on the Biome version, and "file must contain a default export" is an absence check that Grit may not be able to express. Agent Ember must prove each rule fires on a deliberately bad fixture. If a rule can't be expressed, Ember reports it and proposes the closest enforceable rule (for example, banning `export default function` and `export const Foo =` in component files). Ember does not silently skip it.
94:## 5. Agents and models
98:**Workers: all Sonnet.** Each is defined in `.claude/agents/<name>.md` with `model: sonnet`, a distinct `color`, and a codename, so they show up distinguishable in the terminal. The Agent tool can't set a color per call, so the definition files carry it. New agent definitions may need a session restart to load.
110:### Ownership (exclusive write; no agent touches another's files)
115:| **atlas**       | everything under `src/`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | ember done         | Layout renders routes; each route and the layout is its own chunk; `lint`, `typecheck`, `build` pass; every component follows §4                          |
