Redesign calculator UI as a responsive two-column planning dashboard
## Context
The calculator page is a single-column stack of about 12 unrelated cards: one long form, then separate result cards (monthly estimate, cash to close, loan summary, tax, costs, PMI, extra payments, ...) that repeat the same values. There is no app header, and the layout is capped at `max-w-3xl`. Design reference: a standalone HTML concept (to be committed as `design/mortgage-calculator-ui.html` in the PR).

This is a **UI/UX change only**. No calculation engine, rounding rule, assumption, validation rule or hook contract changes. Integer-cent math and all existing tests stay as they are.

## Scope
- App header (brand, nav to Calculator / Compare / Refinance), page title and description.
- Desktop (>= 1024 px): two columns. Inputs on the left; on the right a sticky results column with the monthly ownership cost as the primary KPI.
- Monthly ownership cost hero with a payment breakdown (chart + legend). Lender/escrow lines and non-escrow lines stay separate. ARM "Hypothetical rate" labels and reset-risk text are kept.
- Metrics row: loan amount / LTV, cash to close, lifetime interest, so values appear once.
- Inputs grouped: loan basics visible; collapsible advanced sections (taxes/insurance/HOA/PMI, closing costs, extra payments, growth, affordability) using `<details>`.
- Balance-over-time chart (lightweight inline SVG from the existing schedule) and the existing amortization table.
- Assumptions and the PRD section 11 disclaimer kept visible; illustrative vs. entered values stay labeled.
- Stale results (last valid entry shown while a field is invalid) keep a visible warning.

## Mobile and tablet
- Works at 360 px with no horizontal page scroll; single column below 1024 px; inputs 16 px text (no iOS zoom) and >= 44 px targets.
- A compact bar with the monthly total pinned to the bottom on small screens, linking to the results.
- Tables scroll horizontally inside a keyboard-focusable region.

## Accessibility acceptance criteria
- [ ] Every input has a visible label, hint via `aria-describedby`, and errors as `role="alert"` with `aria-invalid`.
- [ ] Visible focus indicators on every control; keyboard order follows the visual order.
- [ ] Segmented controls are real radio groups; collapsibles are `<details>`.
- [ ] Chart has a text alternative and a data table equivalent (the amortization table); no color-only meaning.
- [ ] WCAG AA contrast; zero axe violations on `/calculator` at 360 / 768 / 1280 px.
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected; no decorative animation.
- [ ] Print report (PrintReport) is unchanged.

## Testing
- Existing unit and component tests keep passing; new tests for new interactive behavior (collapsibles, mobile summary bar, chart text alternative, stale warning).
- `yarn check`, `yarn typecheck`, `yarn test`, `yarn build`.
- Browser pass at 1280, 768 and 360 px with before/after screenshots in the PR.

## Out of scope
Calculation changes, new financial features, new dependencies (no chart or UI library), the Compare and Refinance internals (they get the shared header only).

## Dependencies
Related to #32 / PR #75 (accessibility audit); no code overlap expected beyond `Disclaimer`.

## Definition of done
- Branch `feat/<short-kebab-name>` created from `dev`; merged back into `dev` by PR.
- Components follow `CLAUDE.md` (arrow function, default export, no `any`).
- `yarn check:fix`, `yarn typecheck` and `yarn test` pass.

